('virtual-assistant-article-evidence-handoff', 'Create an Evidence Handoff for Virtual Assistant Article Review', 'evidence handoff', 'giving a reviewer enough context to verify a draft without reconstructing the research', 'claim list, source links, quoted context, uncertainty, requested decision, and version', 'The assistant prepares the handoff; the accountable reviewer decides whether wording is supportable.'),
('virtual-assistant-blog-claim-changes', 'Track Claim Changes During Virtual Assistant Blog Revisions', 'claim changes', 'making material changes visible when an article moves through review', 'old wording, new wording, reason, evidence, affected links, and reopened checks', 'Support can compare versions; editorial authority approves changed public claims.'),
('virtual-assistant-article-example-boundaries', 'Choose Safe Examples for Virtual Assistant Services Articles', 'example boundaries', 'using examples that clarify a workflow without implying an invented client result', 'scenario label, audience, constraint, lesson, and factual status', 'A virtual assistant can catalog examples; an editor decides whether presentation could mislead readers.'),
('virtual-assistant-blog-review-routing', 'Route Virtual Assistant Blog Reviews by Decision Type', 'review routing', 'sending factual, structural, accessibility, and release questions to the right owner', 'review type, exact question, affected section, evidence, owner, and due decision', 'Routing and reminders are support work; each reviewer retains the judgment assigned to them.'),
('virtual-assistant-article-link-purpose', 'Give Every Internal Link a Purpose in Virtual Assistant Articles', 'link purpose', 'making navigation answer a reader need rather than decorate a paragraph', 'destination promise, surrounding question, anchor meaning, and link status', 'Support can inventory and test links; the editor decides relevance and wording.'),
('virtual-assistant-article-reading-path', 'Design a Reading Path for Practical Virtual Assistant Articles', 'reading path', 'helping a busy reader move from problem to decision without losing the article boundary', 'opening question, evidence sequence, examples, decision point, and next action', 'An assistant can test headings and transitions; the writer protects reasoning and nuance.'),
('virtual-assistant-content-refresh-signal', 'Define Refresh Signals for Virtual Assistant Service Articles', 'refresh signals', 'distinguishing a meaningful change from a routine reminder', 'changed source, broken link, reader confusion, process change, claim risk, and owner', 'Support can monitor signals; the editor decides whether to qualify, revise, retire, or leave copy unchanged.'),
